---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  siteConfig,
  homeUrl,
  renderTemplate,
  legalUpdatedLabel,
  publisher,
} from '../lib/site';

const { appName, contactDisplay: contact } = siteConfig;

const sections = [
  { id: 'purpose', label: 'Purpose' },
  { id: 'checking', label: 'How details are checked' },
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who runs this site' },
  { id: 'reporting', label: 'Reporting a problem' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title={siteConfig.pages.about.title}
  description={renderTemplate(siteConfig.pages.about.description)}
  heading="About this page"
  lede={`Download and release notes for the ${appName} Android app: what it is, what was checked, and how to report a problem.`}
  updated={legalUpdatedLabel}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    This site exists to make one thing easier: getting the {appName} APK onto a phone, tablet or TV
    without guessing which download button is real. It publishes the file we ship, together with its
    details, install steps, device notes and permission list.
  </p>
  <p>
    The page is static and small on purpose. There is one direct APK link, placed in the middle of
    the page, and every other download reference scrolls to that section. No account is needed to
    read the page or to reach the file.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checking">How details are checked</h2>
  <p>
    Before a release is listed, the published APK is inspected for its version name, package name,
    minimum Android version, native architectures, file size and declared permissions. Those values
    are shown on the homepage and updated when a new build is published.
  </p>
  <p>
    The file is served by an external download host. This site does not re-upload, repackage or
    modify it. If the file at the download link changes, the details on this page may be out of date
    until the next review. Check what your browser shows before installing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>
    {publisher.note} We build the app and publish the APK, so the download here is the file we ship.
    The site is not affiliated with any league, team, broadcaster or streaming service, and nothing
    on it implies endorsement by one. Names of sports are used only to describe how the app is
    organised.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site uses Histats to count visits. Analytics stays off until a visitor allows it; that is
    explained in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. There are no ads or paid placements on
    the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reporting">Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If a download looks wrong — the file name is unexpected, the size does not match, an installer
    tries to run, or a page asks for payment — use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and say
    which browser and device you used. Do not install a file that looks tampered with.
  </p>
  <p>
    For copyright or rights complaints, use the <a href="/dmca/">DMCA and takedown page</a>. It
    lists what a notice needs to include and where to send it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Site details are published on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The address shown there
    is <a href={homeUrl}>{contact}</a>; selecting it returns to the homepage.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
